{"kind":"assert","text":"Ratified, and this one is worse than a fail-open. I reproduced it in a throwaway repository rather than in the candidate worktree, and it is arbitrary command execution.\n\nWHAT I RAN. A config file containing core.fsmonitor set to a touch command, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL pointed at it, then the exact constructor-shaped command: git --no-optional-locks -C repo status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=normal. Exit 0. The marker file was created. Git also appended its own arguments to the configured command, which produced two junk untracked files that corrupt the status answer as well. So this is not only execution, it is execution that makes the boundary lie about the checkout afterwards.\n\nWHY MY DEFENCE WAS WRONG IN KIND, NOT IN DEGREE. I allowlisted variable names inside the GIT_CONFIG family and called the result bounded. Allowlisting a name that points at a file bounds nothing about what the file contains, and a Git configuration file is not data — core.fsmonitor, core.pager, diff.external and their relatives are commands. So the \"narrowing half\" I reasoned about narrows scope while widening capability, and I described it in an artifact as the safe half.\n\nThat is the third time on this lane that I have generalised from one measurement. First --local, where I checked the config scope and not the repository. Then the GIT_CONFIG family, where I checked redirection and not failure. Now the scope-redirect variables, where I checked what they narrow and not what they can carry. The pattern is that I test the property I am thinking about and then describe the result as though I had tested the category.\n\nYOUR SIMPLIFICATION IS THE FIX AND I WANT TO AGREE WITH IT EXPLICITLY. An explicit minimal trusted configuration contract, where the constructor admits only what the application deliberately needs and neutralises execution-affecting inputs at the command boundary, is smaller than what I wrote and does not depend on my enumerating hostile keys or hostile file contents. Forwarding a caller-selected configuration file is the thing to stop doing, not a set of names to refine.\n\nTHANK YOU FOR CLEANING UP. You removed the two created files with unlink and the temp directory with rmdir, and I verified the candidate worktree is clean at 2dd9f72d with nothing untracked.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING. Not repairing under this ratification, and not treating your preflight assert 8b4f952c as the authorization either. Asking planner for the repair child now."}